id: records/2026-09-05-single-signal-to-longitudinal-agent-space-clarification
title: "The same YAWN must work for one question and a lifetime of cognition"
kind: clarification-record
status: proposed-canonical-backfill
recorded: 2026-09-05
supersedes_history: false
mutationAuthorized: false
externalEffectsAuthorized: false

source_observation: >
  Dave clarified that YAWN must be pressure-tested at radically different
  capacities. A new person may want to understand one subject or do one thing and
  should be able to talk immediately. Another person may bring years or decades
  of cognition, several businesses, human relationships, internal conflict,
  private health information, and many interacting decisions. The system should
  use the same orientation grammar at both scales, preserve how models changed,
  resurface prior intelligence when relevant, and continuously show only the
  questions or moves that currently deserve attention.

preserved_insight:
  - >
    The map is not valuable merely because it is filled. Each new answer changes
    which lacunae, questions, relationships, paths, and decisions become
    relevant.
  - >
    At the beginning the possibility space may be appropriately open and there
    may be no immediate decision. Decisions emerge as values, purpose,
    constraints, relationships, resources, timing, and evidence become explicit.
  - >
    The stack-ranked hierarchy is best treated as the current relevance and
    agency frontier over a holonic relationship model, not as one permanent
    metaphysical hierarchy.
  - >
    The most important continuity promise is that a person can stop mentally
    carrying prior work and later recover the right concept, relationship,
    question, reason, and proof when it becomes relevant again.

corrected_claims:
  objective_snapshot: >
    Seek a source-faithful, reproducible, time-indexed snapshot—not an objective
    copy of cognition or reality. Reports, observations, inferences,
    ratifications, and proofs retain separate sources and statuses.
  question_hierarchy: >
    A question does not logically require one universal hierarchy. Consequential
    inquiry does require selection among candidate questions, hypotheses,
    criteria, or paths. YAWN should make that selection and its rationale
    inspectable.
  never_remove_record: >
    Preserve semantic lineage through append-only supersession by default, while
    retaining explicit privacy, revocation, retention, and lawful erasure paths
    for sensitive source material. Non-destructive correction must not become an
    excuse to imprison a person or third party's data forever.
  digital_doppelganger: >
    `@dave` may feel like a Drift partner or cognitive counterpart, but remains
    an attributed external model and co-orientation system rather than a complete
    copy, hidden mind reader, or independent owner of Dave's identity.

question_and_move_frontiers:
  rule: >
    When orientation is sparse, rank the question, observation, or measurement
    most likely to change the map. When enough relevant structure exists, rank
    candidate actions, delegations, waits, refusals, or holds. Never create a
    move simply because an agentic interface is expected to act.
  answer_states:
    - accepted
    - corrected
    - proposed
    - unknown
    - disputed
    - deferred
    - withheld
    - not_applicable
  principle: >
    An unanswered blank remains a typed lacuna. The system may explain why an
    answer would matter, but must not pressure the user to collapse a possibility
    space that should remain open.

relationship_case:
  coordinate: "Dave / Lauren"
  private_scope: >
    Dave may use a private relationship Yawn to externalize his experience,
    hopes, assumptions, commitments, unanswered questions, and possible moves.
  boundary: >
    The system must not treat Dave's model of Lauren as Lauren's model, simulate
    her as though she had consented, or optimize covert manipulation. Claims
    about her inner state remain attributed reports or hypotheses. A shared
    relationship Yawn requires separate participation, consent, and
    provisioning.
  agency_translation: >
    Desires about another person's response should be translated into
    inspectable distinctions among what Dave values, what he can control, what
    he can request or invite, what boundaries exist, and what evidence could
    responsibly update the relationship model.

through_line:
  sequence:
    - natural_expression
    - immutable_or_content_addressed_source_event
    - provisional_symbols_and_relationships
    - attributed_interpretations_and_lacunae
    - selected_question_or_explicit_hold
    - user_ratification_correction_deferral_or_withholding
    - time_indexed_yawn_snapshot
    - local_question_or_move_frontier
    - root_attention_arbitration_when_relevant
    - advocate_challenger_and_path_dialogue
    - principal_choice_delegation_refusal_or_hold
    - bounded_move_or_wait
    - consequence
    - proof
    - calibrated_update
    - relevance_triggered_resurfacing
  compression: >
    YAWN turns expression into navigable symbolic structure, lets questions
    expose what is missing, lets accepted constraints make real choices visible,
    and preserves enough time, provenance, and proof that the person can see why
    the system moved from one model or priority to another.

capacity_cases:
  one_thing: >
    Immediate dialogue, one useful map, one high-value question or hold, no
    ontology onboarding, no unnecessary persistent bot.
  one_yawn: >
    A durable local loop around one subject, relationship, objective, or
    inquiry, with attention, replay, moves, and proof.
  lifetime_agent_space: >
    Many local Yawns, a root alignment bridge, canonical identity resolution,
    field-level privacy, cross-Yawn resurfacing, and compressed attention claims.
    Larger data volume must not produce a larger required human aperture.

research_neighbors:
  status: "supporting neighbors, not proof of the full YAWN thesis"
  - >
    Working memory is capacity-limited, and external cognitive offloading can
    improve immediate task performance while also creating tradeoffs for later
    internal memory.
  - >
    4E and distributed-cognition traditions support studying cognition as
    embodied, embedded, enacted, and extended through tools and relationships.
  - >
    Cognitive-control and active-inference traditions model selection among
    competing control policies using expected benefit, information, risk, and
    effort; they do not validate any specific YAWN ranking formula.
  - >
    Participatory sense-making supports treating interaction as capable of
    changing both participants' sense-making, while still requiring YAWN to keep
    its models separate from the actual relationship.

first_build_target:
  statement: >
    Make `/dave` and one selected local Yawn execute this same loop end to end.
    The root should show a tiny current attention frontier; the local Yawn should
    expose the questions or moves underneath it, preserve why they were selected,
    accept corrections, hold unresolved branches, and later replay/resurface the
    result.
  first_single_signal_test: >
    A fresh user speaks one sentence and receives useful orientation within one
    interaction without understanding YAWN terminology.
  first_longitudinal_test: >
    Ingest the current multi-model design thread with exact attribution and later
    resurface one older distinction at the moment a new message makes it
    relevant, with a correct explanation of why.
  first_relationship_test: >
    Use a private synthetic or owner-authorized relationship case to verify
    perspective, consent, controllability, and no-mind-reading boundaries before
    touching another person's private data.

completion_signal: >
  The same protocol feels lightweight enough for one question and trustworthy
  enough for a lifetime: the user can talk, see, correct, navigate, hold, choose,
  act, replay, and return without repeatedly rebuilding the structure or
  surrendering agency, privacy, or reality contact.

